  "title": "Bound runner publication inventory to generated output delta",
  "status": "done",
  "milestone": null,
  "dependencies": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "ACC-1: A sealed build inventory contains exactly paths whose index/worktree content changed because of that build, plus its receipt; it must not enumerate every tracked file under a release root.",
    "ACC-2: A committed runner output delta reaches `published` even when an unrelated foreign dirty file exists within a publication root.",
    "ACC-3: A dirty declared output still reaches `publication-pending`; the repair does not weaken detection of uncommitted generated artifacts.",
    "ACC-4: Tests prove both the foreign-WIP counterexample and declared-output fail-closed path. No task-, actor-, filename-, or release-specific allowlist.",
    "ACC-5: Claim admission treats a dirty file outside the candidate task's scope as foreign/unowned WIP unless it is explicitly evidenced as a deliverable of the candidate task; it must not silently add that file to the candidate scope or force an unrelated task-card amendment."
  ],
